From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:05:07 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 26/50] Preview tools: a stuck action no longer wedges its tab

- Agent actions on a tab hold its queue only until their timeout (plus
  500 ms). One still running then is abandoned: its caller fails, the queue
  moves on, held buttons and keys are let go, and a path drag sends nothing
  more. An action whose deadline passed while it waited doesn't start.
- Each mouse event fails after 5 s if the page doesn't take it (a tab that
  stopped drawing frames), with an error that says so, instead of waiting
  for a frame that may never come.
- preview_status reports busy: the running action, and stuck ones.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
